<SupportLayout title="Purchase Terms" eyebrow="SUPPORT / PURCHASES" description="How music, merchandise, and event-related purchases are handled when you visit Perennial Fallout online.">
  <h2>1. About purchases on this website</h2>
  <p>Perennial Fallout's website currently provides band information, music previews, and information about upcoming live shows. <strong>There is no active checkout or payment collection on this website at this time.</strong> A “Buy Track” or merchandise button may indicate that an offering is not yet available. You cannot complete a purchase through this website until a checkout option is expressly enabled.</p>
  <p>If a future purchase option is added, the price, delivery method, payment provider, and terms applicable to that item will be displayed before payment is requested. These terms will be updated when direct online sales become available.</p>
  <h2>2. Purchases through third parties</h2>
  <p>Links to concert tickets, streaming platforms, or music stores may take you to independent websites. Purchases made there are transactions between you and that seller or platform—not purchases completed on perennialfallout.com. Their prices, payment methods, fees, delivery, cancellation, and refund rules apply. Review the third party's terms before completing a transaction.</p>
  <h2>3. Music previews and downloads</h2>
  <p>Music available to play on this site is provided for personal listening and promotional purposes. Streaming or playing a preview does not transfer ownership of the sound recording or grant permission to reproduce, distribute, resell, remix, or publicly exploit the music.</p>
  <p>If the band later offers a downloadable recording through an authorized sales channel, the purchase listing will specify what the buyer receives and any permitted personal-use rights. Copyright in the music and recording remains with its respective rights holders unless expressly stated otherwise.</p>
  <h2>4. Pricing, delivery, and availability</h2>
  <p>Prices and availability shown on third-party services may change without notice. Ticket inventories, venue policies, taxes, processing fees, and digital delivery are determined by the applicable seller. The band's website may link to these services but does not control their checkout systems.</p>
  <h2>5. Refunds, problems, and cancellations</h2>
  <p>For a purchase made through a third-party seller, direct refund, order, or delivery requests to that seller using the confirmation or receipt you received. Refund eligibility is governed by the seller's policies and applicable law.</p>
  <p>If an event is rescheduled or canceled, check the venue or ticket issuer for official information about tickets. Information appearing here is not a guarantee that an event will proceed as listed.</p>
  <h2>6. Questions about an offering</h2>
  <p>For questions about whether a product or download is officially offered by the band, contact <a class="support-email" href="mailto:perennialfallout@gmail.com?subject=Purchase%20Question">perennialfallout@gmail.com</a>. Do not send payment-card details or sensitive financial information by email.</p>
  <div class="support-note"><p><strong>Important:</strong> Purchasing features have not yet launched on this site. This page describes the current arrangement, including outbound links, without suggesting that a checkout or automatic music delivery is already available.</p></div>
</SupportLayout>
